+# Helium browser support
+
+Enable `helium-browser-support` to let ChatGPT Community's Linux browser
+settings find the ChatGPT extension in Helium's `net.imput.helium` profile.
+Helium is preferred for Chrome-family URL and extension-settings actions.
+The integration retains the upstream Chrome family name and extension IDs.
+
+The feature patches the two shared Electron browser registries during a build.
+It preserves other browsers and fails the build if the registry contract changes.
+It does not mark an extension installed without checking its real profile files.
+Browser Control remains a separate integration.
+
+```json
+{ "enabled": ["computer-use-linux", "helium-browser-support"] }
+```
+
+Pass the same feature configuration to codex-update-manager through
+`feature_config_path` to retain the feature in updates. Restart the app after
+installing the rebuilt package.
+
+Run `node --test linux-features/helium-browser-support/test.js`.
